Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:13:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] feat(audit): ship the Audit Hub connector, installed and
 off

Audit Hub keeps a tamper-evident log of a project's security events and
answers "my account's security". This adds its Expo connector
(src/lib/audit/, vendored with `pnpm connector add --kind expo` in Audit
Hub's repository) with every integration point. Without the API's
connector on the other side its routes answer 404, and the app stays
as it was: the account security screen says it is not available.

On, the app queues its own events per user in SQLite (expo-sqlite,
already a dependency) and sends them every 30 s, on foreground and on
reconnect, a sign-out flushing for 3 s at most; every request carries
the installation's id (X-Device-Id) with the version headers. Settings
gains "Account security" (the person's sign-ins and changes, a page at a
time) and answers a "Was it you?" prompt opened from a notification of
the new security channel, the link only opening the screen. The phone's
position goes with a session's start only with a separate, revocable consent
(expo-location, foreground only: app.config.ts blocks the background
permission), when a session starts (a sign-in, or the app opened with
its session kept). The system's dialog lets the person choose: precise,
one fresh fix kept to five decimals; approximate, the last known
position rounded to 0.01 degrees on the device.

The mock API answers the connector's routes; Maestro flows cover events
waiting for the API, sign-out between users and "Was it you?" answered
both ways. The data inventory, store declarations, architecture,
releases and manuals (both languages) describe the new data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
